 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? In Italian, bill looks like bill and sounds like bill, so you can just ask for the bill. You can say we would like a table for two, or un table pour deux, depending on how formal the restaurant is. You can say la cuisine est brilliante, which means the kitchen is brilliant. You got the hang of it. Now go out and enjoy your meal. Say you' like to check the bill please, and point to the sign by the door. Most people do it automatically anyway. You've really got the hang of it. Go enjoy your food.",
